# The agent mirror is drift-guarded BYTE-IDENTICAL against a fresh render
# (src/agent/agentMirror.generated.test.ts), and the generator emits LF. Without
# this pin, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true checks these files out as
# CRLF and the guard false-fails for everyone on that platform — the same class
# of trap as a probe measuring the wrong tree. Same reasoning for the other
# generated artifact.
public/llms.txt text eol=lf
public/agent/*.md text eol=lf
src/pages/about/subBranches.generated.json text eol=lf
# The sitemap is the third generated artifact and shipped on 2026-07-28 without a
# pin here, so `seo.generated.test.ts` false-failed on every Windows clone — the
# diff was every line changed and every line identical, which is what a line-ending
# mismatch looks like and reads as a real drift. Adding a generated file to the
# repo means adding it here too.
public/sitemap.xml text eol=lf
